{"id":"00000001794776354624:79ce3955c2ee186b2e971c9e3dc955c2","text":"Static feature strip validated (TESTED on sim 8CCC71C9): strip5 runtime 93.7 MB vs 0.1.4 149.5 MB (81 features: CLI/tooling plus Bun.*/node server, db, process, socket APIs; web globals kept). One __TEXT exec segment. one-basic, Team Machine, Intl smoke (20 cases) and globals smoke (174 globals materialized) identical to 0.1.4. Removing WebAssembly traps in LLInt::initialize, so it stays. Scripts going into bun-engine relink-macos-embed.py --remove; then v0.1.5 and a One podspec bump. #1258 merged 253a66f70; #1251 fixed by me at d0a6ec1d7 (key scoping, tamagui package registry), merge on green."}

{"id":"00000001794779885104:8601ef5795140a2379ad1fe3e60c6886","text":"Jarred's suggestions (2026-11-15). Bun release link flags (lto-CGO3, whole-program-visibility/vtables, inline-cold-callsite-threshold=0, no-keep-static-consts, icf=safe at LTO and native link): runtime 79.07 MB vs 81.23 MB (TESTED: one-basic, Team Machine launch; Intl 21 lines and globals 29 lines identical on sim 8CCC71C9). Packaged as 0.1.6 at rel-016, bench running. System ICU data instead of bundled: RAN harness, ICU 74 code on iOS 27's icudt78l.dat fails likely subtags, NFKC and IDNA (URL) and breaks ja word segmentation, so not viable; system libicucore linking was rejected by ITMS-90338. Remaining 24 MB ICU data is all reachable from Intl. Built-in module texts (2.7 MB) need Interpreter (eval/new Function) removed, which Hermes keeps, so skipped."}
